  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac a **non-empty** MPStorage document: other clients' namespaces, member pseudos (blacklist), a size near the 64 KiB cap or a non-BMP character. #132 (PR #259) captured the thread page and edit form (`R60a`, `R60b`), but user1's live document is the empty structure the legacy app creates, so LOT-038/052 have no real multi-client document.\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: the MPStorage thread's first-post page and its edit form (`content_form`, exact bytes) for an account whose document already holds other clients' data or pseudos, ideally one near 64 KiB or with a non-BMP character; then the LOT-004 (#41) exporter `mpstorage-page` kind on the page and `form` `edit` on the form.\n\nNote: none exists in the kit's accounts (user1: empty document, user2: no storage thread, `R13a`). Producing one needs a **write** to a document shared with the user's other clients: only with the operator's go (an account that already has such a document, or a dedicated one). The anonymizer refuses any key, string or bare list value it does not know in the document (`MPStorageDocumentError`), so the capture PR first adds aliasing for those positions (blacklist pseudos, other clients' keys), with tests and an independent check.\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it; one PR per batch of captures.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-038 (#65), LOT-052 (#78)\n\n### Depends on\n\n#132\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (needs an operator decision; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\nWhat #132 left pending (PR #259, MANIFEST \"Not captured\", HFR-PROTOCOL \"MPStorage read\" row).\n",
